<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec_force-field0" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
	<title>Applying Forces and Fields</title>

	<assemblage component="implementation">
  <title>Implementation Notes</title>
  <p>
	The activities in this section were designed to be implemented in a 50-minute interactive classroom, after students have completed the rest of the chapter, especially:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<p>
				<xref ref="sec_electric-reps"/>
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p>
				<xref ref="sec_electric-field_point_charge"/>
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p>
				<xref ref="sec_coulomb"/>
			</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
  </assemblage>

  <subsubsection>
	<title>Activities</title>
	
  </subsubsection>

	<activity xml:id="class_000">
		<title>Charge Launcher I</title>
		<introduction>
			<p>
			
		</p>
		<p>
			You decide to make a launcher by gluing a <m>+20 \mathrm{~mC}</m> point charge at the bottom of a vertical tube that is <m>10 \mathrm{~m}</m> long.
		</p>
		</introduction>
		<task>
			<statement>
				<p>
					Make a qualitatively accurate vector map of the electric field in the tube.
				</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
		<task>
			<statement>
				<p>
					Find the magnitude of the electric field in <m>\mathrm{N/C}</m> halfway to the top of the tube.
				</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
		<task>
			<statement>
				<p>
Find the magnitude of the electric field in <m>\mathrm{N/C}</m> at the top of the tube.
				</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
	</activity>

	<activity xml:id="class_001">
		<title>Charge Launcher II</title>
		<introduction>
			<p>
			
		</p>
		<p>
Your projectile for the charge launcher above is a heavy metal ball with mass <m>900 \mathrm{~kg}</m> and charge <m>+5 \mathrm{~mC}</m>. The projectile begins halfway up the tube.
		</p>
		</introduction>
		<task>
			<statement>
				<p>
					Find the net force and acceleration on the projectile at its starting point.
				</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
		<task>
			<statement>
				<p>
					As the projectile moves, is the acceleration constant?  At what point, if any, is the acceleration zero? What does this mean for the projectile?
				</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
	</activity>

